    "blurb": "The late set blends acoustic country numbers with a fiery second half. Highlights include Dire Wolf’s pedal‑steel charm, the swirling Dark Star → Saint Stephen → The Eleven sequence, and a crisp Turn On Your Lovelight. The soundboard capture is crystal clear, making this a must‑listen for early Dead fans.",
    "review": "June 21, 1969 at the Fillmore East finds the Grateful Dead in a transitional groove – folk‑country storytelling meets the psychedelic stretch that would soon define their live mythos. Jerry’s sweet pedal‑steel on “Dire Wolf” and his emerging Strat tone weave through acoustic gems like “Old, Old House,” “Mama Tried,” and “High Time.” The band then launches into a seamless marathon: Dark Star → Saint Stephen → The Eleven, showcasing Phil’s steady bass foundation and the twin‑drum engine of Mickey and Bill driving the intensity. The set closes with a sparkling rendition of “Turn On Your Lovelight,” captured in pristine soundboard quality that lets every nuance shine. While an audience matrix recording of the first half exists, it is muddy; the superior SBD (gd1969-06-21.sbd‑late.bove.2195.sbeok.shnf) presents a complete, crystal‑clear picture of this historic night.",
